{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":97658,"duration_api_ms":97619,"num_turns":12,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f46e7044-4a16-440d-b463-c3d514edd8b3","total_cost_usd":0.3940922499999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29363,"cache_read_input_tokens":185077,"output_tokens":4720,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29363,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":7,"outputTokens":4720,"cacheReadInputTokens":185077,"cacheCreationInputTokens":29363,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3940922499999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Evaluated amendment fr-3-95d007dd concerning gas-exchange scaling. The amendment correctly identifies a physical modeling error: gas exchange at the air-water interface depends on surface area, not water volume. The current code computes K_LA without the A/V term, then multiplies by volume, making total mass transfer proportional to volume instead of surface area. The test at co2_exchange.rs:215-285 locks in this incorrect behavior. The geometry module already has the needed surface_area_to_gross_volume_ratio() helper. Both O2 and CO2 paths are affected.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-3-95d007dd","decision":"accept","rationale":"The amendment correctly identifies a physical modeling error. Gas exchange is a surface-area-driven process: total flux = kL × A × (C_eq - C). The current code's compute_o2_kla() returns a flat coefficient (no A/V term), yet the exchange formula multiplies by volume_l, making total mass transfer scale with volume instead of surface area. Two tanks sharing the same footprint but differing in fill height would incorrectly exchange different total CO2/O2 masses. The test at lines 215-285 asserts equal concentration change (volume-independent), but physically the shallower tank (higher A/V ratio) should equilibrate faster. The geometry.rs:66 helper surface_area_to_gross_volume_ratio() already exists and is the correct scaling factor to incorporate. Both O2 (dissolved_oxygen.rs:68) and CO2 (chemistry.rs:580) paths need the fix."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"c0ec1483-bba6-4589-a2af-c46e15805b77"}
